    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a young fox character. Draw this exact fox as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the body: the orange fluffy body with its cream chest, upright as in image 1, without head, legs or tail; its top, normally under the head, rounded.\n2. the head: the fox's head with its cream cheeks and black nose, facing right as in image 1, with a completely blank face — no eyes, no mouth — keep the nose and the rosy cheeks; without ears; its bottom edge rounded.\n3. one ear: a pointed orange ear with cream fluff inside and a dark tip, with a rounded base.\n4. one front leg: the front leg on the right of image 1, held up with its dark paw, with a rounded shoulder.\n5. one hind leg: the near hind leg with its dark foot, with a rounded hip.\n6. the tail: the big fluffy white-tipped tail, with a rounded base.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or the head) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a young fox character; image 2 shows the same fox cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the fox's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the fox in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the fox's left eye (on the right of image 1) as it is in image 1: a dark round eye with a white sparkle.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: looking down, its upper lid tilted up towards the middle.\n6. the mouth as it is in image 1: open in a bright happy grin, the inside pink.\n7. the mouth closed in a small calm smile.\n8. the mouth wide open in a big happy laugh, the inside pink.\n9. the mouth open in a small round 'o'.\n10. the mouth in a small sad frown.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
